You are a senior enterprise AI architect.

We need to build a production-oriented enterprise AI application using Python, RAG, LLMs and tool/API integration.

Business scenario:

The enterprise has very large and heterogeneous data sources:

PDFs and documents
SharePoint/Confluence-style knowledge bases
CSV/JSON files
relational databases
enterprise APIs
Jira/incidents
technical documentation

There are also many REST APIs for real-time information such as customers, accounts, transactions, payments and operational data.

The application must support natural-language queries and determine whether the query should use:

Vector RAG
Hybrid RAG
Enterprise API/tool
A combination of RAG + APIs

Requirements:

Design a production-grade architecture before writing implementation code.
Create an architecture/design document explaining:
system components
data flow
ingestion architecture
retrieval architecture
query routing
API/tool routing
context construction
LLM generation
security
authorization
observability
evaluation
scalability
failure handling
caching
cost optimization
Use hybrid retrieval:
vector search
keyword/BM25 search
result fusion
reranking
metadata filtering
Design ingestion for very large datasets:
batch processing
incremental ingestion
deduplication
document versioning
metadata
asynchronous processing
embedding caching
Do NOT put transactional or real-time API data into the vector database unnecessarily.
Create a tool/API registry so that hundreds of enterprise APIs can be represented as controlled tools.
Implement a query router that classifies requests as:
KNOWLEDGE
REAL_TIME_DATA
TRANSACTIONAL/API
HYBRID
Implement role/tenant/access-control metadata filtering before retrieval.
Never rely on the LLM alone for authorization.
Include citations/source attribution for RAG responses.
Add hallucination and groundedness checks.
Add structured logging, tracing and latency/token/cost metrics.
Add evaluation for:
retrieval precision
retrieval recall
MRR/Recall@K
answer faithfulness
answer relevance
citation correctness
routing accuracy
API/tool success rate
Design the application so that components can be independently scaled.
Use clean interfaces so vector DB, embedding model, LLM and reranker can be replaced without major application changes.
Include unit tests, integration tests and representative evaluation datasets.

Before implementing:

Step 1:
Inspect the repository and existing files.

Step 2:
Create an architecture/design document.

Step 3:
Create the proposed project structure.

Step 4:
Explain key design decisions and trade-offs.

Step 5:
Wait for approval before implementing the complete application.

Do not prematurely write large amounts of implementation code.
Prioritize enterprise architecture, modularity, security, scalability and testability.
